## Database

The `db` component in `config/components/db.rb` is a SQLite database under `storage/`, which classes reach with `dep :db`.

```sh
bin/sid db migrations add create_things   # writes db/migrations/<timestamp>_create_things.rb
bin/sid db migrations run
bin/sid db migrations rollback            # just the one that ran last
```
<% if sourced? -%>

Sourced keeps the app's commands and events in the same database, in tables its own migration creates — `bin/sid sourced install` wrote it. `bin/sid sourced topology` shows how the app's commands, events and read models connect.
<% end -%>
<% end -%>

## Layout

| Path | What's in it |
| --- | --- |
| `boot.rb` | Loads and configures the app |
| `config/components/` | Components: the connections, clients and other services the app's classes use, declared with `Sidereal.config`. `boot.rb` loads every file here. See `example.rb`, and `secrets.rb`, which gives Sidereal the app's master secret, that it derives the keys for the session cookie and for signing the URLs of pages' live updates from, and `assets.rb`, which says how layouts link the app's assets |
| `system/` | Backend code that doesn't know about the web: messages, commanders, Sourced deciders and reactors, and components (see below) |
| `web/app.rb` | `App`, the web app: its pages, and the background handlers of commands |
| `web/ui/` | Pages and the layout, in the `UI` namespace. A page declares the commands its forms send with `handle` |
| `web/ui/components/` | Components used by pages, in `UI::Components` |
| `web/assets/` | Stylesheets, scripts and images. `App` registers the directory, and the layout links its stylesheets and scripts. See `config/components/assets.rb` |
<% if database? -%>
| `db/migrations/` | Database migrations, run with `bin/sid db migrations run`. Add one with `bin/sid db migrations add <name>` |
<% end -%>
| `storage/` | Runtime data<% if database? %>, including the SQLite database<% end %>, and `secret.txt`, the app's secret unless `SIDEREAL_SECRET` is set. Not committed. |
| `falcon.rb` | Falcon server settings |
| `.env` | Optional: environment variables for development. `boot.rb` loads it, if there is one, and variables already set win. Not committed. |
| `bin/dev` | Development server that reloads on code changes |
| `bin/sid` | Sidereal's command line with this app loaded. `bin/sid --help` lists its commands, e.g. `bin/sid console` |
| `.agents/skills/` | Skills that teach AI coding agents to work with this app, such as using `bin/sid`. `.claude/skills` links here, for Claude Code. `bin/sid skills update` refreshes the ones Sidereal and its integrations provide |

Classes in `system/` and `web/` are loaded by [Zeitwerk](https://github.com/fxn/zeitwerk): name a file after the class it defines and use the class anywhere, without `require`. Directories under `web/` are namespaces, so `web/ui/welcome_page.rb` defines `UI::WelcomePage`. Classes in `system/` are top-level.

A class in a directory under `system/` that includes `Sourced::Component::Installable` is a component, keyed by its path, so any class can ask for it with `dep`:

```ruby
# system/mailers/client.rb: the mailers.client component
class Mailers::Client
  include Sourced::Component::Installable
  extend Sidereal::Deps
  dep 'mailers.templates' # built with the components it asks for

  def deliver(to:)
    # ...
  end
end

# web/app.rb
class App < Sidereal::App
  dep 'mailers.client' # a `client` reader
end
```

One process builds one instance, when it starts. A file directly in `system/`, like `greetings.rb`, can't be a component. Each directory owns its key, so don't declare `mailers.*` components in `config/components/` too: they're dropped. And a class loaded from `config/components/`, such as a decider passed to `Sourced.register`, loads before the `system/` components are declared, so it can't `dep` one. With Sourced installed, the deciders and projectors in `system/` are registered by the same scan that declares those components, so they can.
